 2022-2023a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2021-2022a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2020-2021a.y. Close Career Services Section Menu Overview Career Guidance & Approaching the Job Market Overview Career Guidance Approaching the Job Market Meet with employers Overview Bespoke events Career fairs JobGate: applying online Your internship: from start to recognition Overview Guide to curricular internships Guide to extracurricular internships Close Breadcrumb Home For Current Students Career Services Contacts Career Services Open share Close Share Close Bocconi Career Services support students and graduates as they enter the job market , providing tools and advice to help them reach their professional goals. Close ties with the business community and organizations have enabled successful partnerships with employers , allowing the recruitment of qualified talents . With the goal of fostering contacts between students and employers worldwide, Bocconi Career Services organize a portfolio of activities related to recruiting, networking and career counseling , available throughout the academic year. Available Career Services Career Guidance & Approaching the Job Market Tools and initiatives to support your first approach to the job market Meet with employers Meet with single employers on bespoke events, or engage with a range of employers during career fairs JobGate: applying online Bocconi’s online portal to find an internship or a job Your internship: from start to credit recognition Activate and manage your internship with the support of Bocconi's Internship Office Placement of Bocconi Graduates 94.7% MSc graduates employed 1 year after graduation 36% employed abroad Bocconi and Employers in 2025 16 career fairs in Italy and abroad, with 700+ participating employers 740+ employers involved in meetings with students and graduates 9,300+ internship and job opportunities posted online Associate Employer network Corporate Associate Program A2A LIFE COMPANY B